# .dockerignore for the self-contained multi-stage Dockerfile (not the
# scaffolded host-build packages/backend/Dockerfile). The multi-stage
# build needs full source trees (packages/*/src, plugins/) so it can
# compile + bundle inside docker — exclusions must preserve those.
#
# Excludes:
#   .git             — git metadata; never needed at build time
#   node_modules     — regenerated inside docker via `yarn install`
#   .yarn/cache      — yarn's local cache; rebuilt via BuildKit mount cache
#   .yarn/install-state.gz — ephemeral yarn install state
#   *.local.yaml     — developer-local app-config overrides
#
# Deliberately NOT excluded (so builder stage can see them):
#   packages/*/src   — frontend + backend TypeScript source
#   plugins/         — workspace plugin dirs (even if empty, yarn
#                      workspaces discovery expects the path)
#   examples/        — sample catalog data (shipped as part of the
#                      runtime image for the sample Backstage experience)

.git
.yarn/cache
.yarn/install-state.gz
node_modules
*.local.yaml
